<Legal
  title="Accessibility | Let's Dimsum, San Pablo City, Laguna"
  heading="Accessibility statement"
  description="How the Let's Dimsum website is built to be usable by everyone, the accessibility standard we aim for, and how to tell us about a problem."
>
  <p>Last updated: [date of lawyer review]</p>

  <h2>Our aim</h2>
  <p>We want everyone to be able to read our menu and find us. We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>

  <h2>What we've done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The whole site works with a keyboard, with a visible focus outline.</li>
    <li>Every photo has a text description.</li>
    <li>The full menu is plain text, not an image, and also available as a PDF.</li>
    <li>If your device is set to reduce motion, animations and smooth scrolling are turned off.</li>
    <li>All content is readable with JavaScript turned off.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limits</h2>
  <p>The downloadable menu PDF is a scan of the printed board, so it isn't screen-reader friendly. The menu on this site has the same items as text.</p>

  <h2>Tell us about a problem</h2>
  <p>If something doesn't work for you, contact us at [email address] or on our Facebook page and we'll help.</p>
</Legal>
